{
  "$schema": "nbidal18/config-classification/1",

  "$doc": [
    "Every managed file under config/ must be classified here. Build-PackwizSite.ps1 fails the",
    "build if any config file is unclassified, so adding a mod forces a deliberate decision",
    "instead of silently inheriting hash enforcement.",
    "",
    "Classes:",
    "  gameplay - in-game content. Hash-enforced at runtime; editing it refuses the login.",
    "  support  - library, performance, rendering, UI, input or diagnostic config. Not in-game",
    "             content, so the runtime monitor ignores it. The pre-launch updater still",
    "             restores the published copy, so content stays deterministic without ever",
    "             producing a lockout.",
    "  player   - genuinely player-owned settings. Published once, preserved forever, never",
    "             checked. Adding one here means we can no longer update that file.",
    "",
    "Longest matching prefix wins. A rule ending in / matches a directory subtree.",
    "Files outside config/ are enforced unless listed explicitly.",
    "",
    "modWritesAtRuntime marks a gameplay config the owning mod rewrites during its own startup.",
    "It does NOT exempt the file - it stays fully enforced. It records an obligation: the file must",
    "be published in the exact form the mod writes back, so the rewrite is byte-identical and no",
    "false alarm results. Measured on a played instance, all of them currently are.",
    "",
    "When updating one of these mods, launch once, let it rewrite the config, and take that as the",
    "new master. Test-ConfigStability.ps1 fails the release if a flagged file no longer round-trips.",
    "If a gameplay config ever genuinely varies per machine or per session, do not exempt the whole",
    "file: use propertyRules to pin the specific keys that matter, the way GLOWING_ORE_MASTER is",
    "pinned inside an otherwise player-owned shader settings file."
  ],

  "extraTolerantRoots": [
    {
      "prefix": "config",
      "reason": [
        "Unmanaged extra files under config/ are tolerated instead of refusing the login.",
        "config/ is not a loadable-content root: mods, datapacks, resourcepacks and shaderpacks",
        "stay exact-match, and those are the only roots Minecraft loads code or content from.",
        "Every managed config file is still hash-checked according to its class above, so",
        "tampering with gameplay config is still caught - only genuinely new files are ignored.",
        "",
        "This exists because config libraries write their own files during mod init. Cristel Lib",
        "creates config/cristellib/<mod>/ for every structure mod, CryonicConfig and several",
        "others do the same. Those files cannot be allowlisted in advance: the pre-launch updater",
        "deletes them, the game recreates them at startup, and the player is locked out with no",
        "way to clear it. That happened on the chisel config in 4.1.x and on Nullscape in 4.2.0.",
        "",
        "Before adding a mod that loads content from a config subdirectory (Paxi, OpenLoader,",
        "YOSBR and similar), narrow this to explicit prefixes - none are installed today."
      ]
    }
  ],

